    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, just finished a rumenotomy on one of my heifers. need a protocol for the next few days to make sure she recovers okay. specifically what should i be looking for regarding infection and when can i start bringing her back onto feed? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Immediately after the rumenotomy, closely monitor your heifer for signs of depression, decreased appetite, or suspicious behavior, as these may indicate discomfort or possible infection. Watch for excessive heat stress, abnormal white blood cell counts, or changes in stool consistency, which could be early signs of infection. You can start bringing her back onto feed gradually, but do not rush. If she does not seem to be feeling well, consult a veterinarian urgently for potential antibiotics or other appropriate treatments. Ensure she has access to plenty of fresh, clean water and watch for any drastic changes. Regularly check her vital signs and consider a fecal egg count test to monitor her internal parasite load, especially if you're resuming more intense activity.",
