    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah that makes sense. i'm mostly just worried about those hidden issues that start small and then just explode out of nowhere. like, is there any way to tell if there's something lurking or creeping in that isn't showing up on the surface yet? just want to stay ahead of it before it gets bad.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To keep ahead of potentially hidden issues, maintain a high level of observation and care. Regularly check the surgical incursion through non-invasive means, such as ultrasound, if recommended by your veterinarian, to detect early signs of abscess formation or other hidden complications. Routinely monitor her respiratory rate, heart rate, and mucous membranes for any subtle changes that could indicate systemic issues. Perform a thorough and consistent examination of the rumen, including auscultation to listen for abnormal sounds or rumen contractions that might indicate instability or herniation within the abdominal cavity. If routine health checks reveal abnormalities, consider diagnostic imaging or endoscopic procedures as directed by your veterinarian. Early detection through frequent and detailed monitoring can prevent issues from escalating.",
